P6-4: teacher-submitted video links

Board feedback: PDFs and articles exist, but study videos only live in a
Telegram group serving both JAMB and 100-level students, so they are hard
to organize. Hosting clarified to Google Drive, submitted by Teachers.

A link is not an upload. AGENTS.md §3 and DESIGN.md §6 previously made
content_items Admin-only outright; the reading adopted is that the rule
governs uploads (files landing in Supabase Storage), so Teachers
submitting video links honours the decision as written while pdf and
article uploads stay Admin-only. Both docs amended with that reasoning
rather than silently deviated from.

- content_type gains 'video' (migration 0006, applied).
- lib/content/video-link.ts normalises a pasted URL at READ time, so the
  URL is stored exactly as given and improving the parser improves every
  existing link. Drive /view is rewritten to /preview because Google
  refuses to frame /view - embedding the URL a teacher actually copies
  renders a blank box that looks like it loaded. Also handles /open?id=,
  drive.usercontent, YouTube (watch/youtu.be/shorts/embed) and Telegram;
  folders and Telegram posts get embedUrl null. Rejects non-http(s)
  schemes, so javascript: and data: URLs can never be stored and rendered
  as an href.
- /api/teacher/resources + /[id]: admin+teacher, ownership-scoped, and
  the create schema hard-codes type 'video' so a Teacher cannot reach
  pdf/article through this endpoint. /api/admin/content gains a video
  track for admins.
- Videos are exempt from the /api/resources active-semester filter, so a
  recorded lecture survives the Harmattan->Rain rollover while PDFs and
  articles still expire.
- UI: /teacher/resources + a "Videos" nav item, a "Video link" tab on
  /admin/content, and a video row on /resources whose player iframe
  mounts only on tap (an always-on iframe per row would burn mobile data
  on load for an audience that is mostly on phones).

Verified: 651 tests pass, pnpm lint 0 errors, pnpm typecheck clean, and
pg_enum read back as pdf, article, video after db:migrate.

